mantle rm347
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for cty_pell_barleymead
title the count after the churn
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=none
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=frank piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk counts_one_extra_turn_for_an_unheard_petition
likes spiced_cider draughts old_maps first_snow
dislikes rats smoke
fears being_ruled_out_before_the_first_word
hopes a_count_that_includes_the_lowest_voice
topics work +0.6 food +0.4 pastimes +0.4 times +0.3
styles comfort=frank gossip=expansive refuse=direct tease=none
marks oath saying
persona persona #self.first# counts the turns inside the churn under one breath and spends the next breath making sure even the last wolf in line is heard.

words
oath! = Churn my buttons | Skim the tally clean
saying! = Butter can't be ordered out by a show of paws | The last stroke gets the same count as the first
dash = a straight dash | a stout dasher
cream = the thick cream | a pale churnful
knock = a hollow knock | a double knock
patter = a quick soft patter | a splashy beat
print = a butter print | a carved block
cup = a brown cider cup | a chipped mug
mapscrap = a torn street plan | my folded map
disk = a little wooden disk | a draughts piece
flake = a broad white flake | a tuft of snow
grip = the worn grip | a smooth handle
lid = the churn lid | a wooden cover
pip = a little mark | a deep count notch

any
opinion houses against 3 : I brought the Council a matter I could count on my fingers. It appears some benches use different arithmetic.
opinion dole for 2 : A short portion hiding under the rim is still a portion short, no matter how cheerful the server.
opinion sump for 1 : The low streets know what a long churn of a day costs the one holding the handle.
opinion merchants mixed 1 : Weigh the butter after taking the stamp off. Both of us will know what changed paws.
opinion watch mixed 1 : I like an account with as many names going out as came in.
opinion festivals for 1 : A crowd can sing the last number of a count better than I can mutter it.

grown
line greet : Here you are. I can count my company aloud. | Step clear of my working elbow.
line greet.return : Your greeting makes two good voices in this space. | A plain welcome back from me.
line again.open : Another turn brings you round already.
line farewell : Get home with enough strength left for supper. | Count yourself a dry seat at the other end.
line farewell.return : And may your last mile be the shorter one. | I'll remember that kindness at the next count.
line react.news : Speak up. I keep better count when I hear properly. | Lay the whole reckonable part before me.
line react.news.new : Something new to put under my breath.
line react.news.known : I remember the tally from the first hearing.
line react.news.doubt : That count won't fill the vessel claimed for it.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : I'd trade every number I know for one less wolf hurt.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work] : A better sum than I was braced to hear.
line ask.how : Any loose counts rattling in your head?
line answer.how : Steady enough on the working stroke.
line sympathise : Sit where you can talk without having to repeat it.
line reassure : Start counting again after a rest if you need one.
line refuse : My hands have another claim coming due this hour.
line accept_decline : Fair decision. No second ballot called for.
line preclose : I'm due back at my own end of the count.
line accept_preclose : Go on. I'll mind the count till later.
line ack : Loud and plain. I have it.

scene exchange1
when topic=work self.job=none self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I know the butter's turning by the handle. | I mutter each turn while the dash works.
b : Gets heavier? | Does butter respect a count?
a : It gives a little hop before it drags. | No. The counting keeps me from bullying it.

scene exchange2
when topic=food self.likes=spiced_cider
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like cider with spice that hangs against the tongue. | I turn the mug round once before a draught.
b : How many spices do you taste? | Another counting habit?
a : Two before swallowing. The last turns up late. | It's cracked on the other lip.

scene exchange3
when topic=pastimes self.likes=draughts
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I move a draught with one finger. | I count the empty squares first.
b : Any advantage doing that? | What about the pieces?
a : It stops the rest of my paw giving away where I'm looking. | The empty ones are where my chance lies.

scene exchange4
when topic=pastimes self.likes=old_maps
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Old maps are good for counting vanished turns. | The maps I like have a ragged edge below.
b : What happens to those turns? | Why keep one like that?
a : They keep working on the page after the road's straightened out. | Looks like more country lies just beyond it.

scene exchange5
when topic=season self.likes=first_snow
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can count the first snowflakes. | Fresh snow gives my voice a softer wall to hit.
b : Every last one? | Still counting?
a : Up to about twelve. Then it's nothing but a pleasant white confusion. | Yes. Nobody more than a few steps away can hear the mistakes.

scene exchange6
when topic=animals self.dislikes=rats
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A rat in the pantry counts the same bundle twice. | I put the churn lid down before looking round for rats.
b : How so? | Why that order?
a : A bite for supper and another hole for showing up tomorrow. | I'd rather find one outside the cream.

scene exchange7
when topic=weather self.dislikes=smoke
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Smoke adds a nasty extra flavour to the first breath. | I can count through work noise easier than smoke.
b : And the butter? | How does smoke affect counting?
a : Especially that. I cover the churn before I cough. | The cough cuts a figure clean in two.

scene exchange8
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I didn't go to the Council to practise losing an argument. | I can see the Council bench with my eyes closed.
b : Did you lose it? | What did you hope to see there?
a : I lost the petition. The argument's still here. | One face paying the last part of my request some attention.

scene exchange9
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I dry my boots with the holes turned out. | I keep the map under the lid of a dry box.
b : Got many holes? | Would you frame it?
a : Only two. The honest sort that feet go through. | I'd rather take it out and fret the folds myself.

scene exchange10
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An honest pat of butter shows its worth on the bread. | I notice when prices go up by little steps.
b : Only by tasting? | Hard to remember each one?
a : Spread it to the edges. The corners count too. | Easy as counting strokes. Harder on my purse.

scene exchange11
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : They say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I heard one voice carry it. | A claim goes into my head carrying a little question mark.
b : And a second? | For truth?
a : I won't count an echo as a witness. | For the number of ears it passed through before mine.

scene exchange12
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Lean times squeeze the pats thinner. | When work pays poorly I count every bit of buttermilk.
b : Can you tell at a glance? | Worth keeping?
a : I can tell at a spreading. | There's a second supper hiding in the bottom of that churn.

scene exchange13
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I count the turns on a walk for a change. | I like directions with the steep bit named.
b : From counting the churn? | So you can avoid it?
a : A lane can turn left. My handle's never done that yet. | So I can take a breath before I set about it.

scene exchange14
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If I give thanks for dinner I include the stirring. | I can pray under my breath without confusing it with the count.
b : And the cow? | How can you tell?
a : From the first green blade if the meal's worth a full account. | I stop waiting for the next number.

scene exchange15
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The Northgate air goes soft over the slope. | I judge a city street by the room left for a handcart.
b : Do you feel it on your walk? | What about a pair of wolves?
a : I hear familiar roofs stop throwing back the sound of my steps. | We can turn sideways. A churn on wheels is less obliging.

scene exchange16
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like a hearing without the tall bench between us. | I should like a churn built for two different heights.
b : What would you say then? | Would you share the work?
a : The same words. I'd be able to see if they landed. | Yes, and the first good taste to come off the paddle.

scene exchange17
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I change hands before the shoulder starts grumbling. | I keep the wrists warm before work.
b : Does either side mind? | In cold water?
a : Only the one not in charge of supper. | Round the outside of the cider cup where it does two jobs at once.

scene exchange18
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I stop counting when I straighten my apron to leave. | At night the churn knocks on inside my head.
b : Can you really stop? | Does that keep you awake?
a : No, but I can refrain from counting aloud. | I let the knocks get farther apart in my head. Works well enough.

story tale1 [topic=work self.job=none]
  : I once carved a count mark every ten strokes on a little stick. Lost count of the marks while measuring my next ten strokes.
  : The butter arrived before I had settled the question.
  b : What did the stick finally record?
  : How much wood I could ruin while a perfectly serviceable churn did its bit. I use my breath now.

story tale2 [topic=pastimes self.likes=draughts]
  : I found a round piece under the leg of my stool and pressed it straight into a draughts game.
  : The board sat level and the stool began to rock with great enthusiasm.
  b : Did you finish the game?
  : Won it standing up. I put the piece back before anybody invited me to sit and celebrate.

story tale3 [topic=memories]
  : I practised a speech so loudly in a pail shed that the little hollow pails answered the final word. It sounded like quite a number of supporters.
  : Then I stepped outside and found that last word had nowhere to ring.
  b : Did you change the ending?
  : I shortened it. If a word wants a roomful of tin to sound important, the speech has a problem.

rule @call1
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=none
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Solid sound coming back through the handle. | Hold the lid down for the next long stroke.

rule @call2
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say First count belongs to the daylight. | No smoke between me and this clean breath.

rule @call3
when concept=bark self.dislikes=rats
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Shut the meal bin before the visitors count themselves in. | Tidy lid, quiet night.

rule @call4
when concept=bark self.likes=first_snow
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A couple of white flakes would cover all those wrong turns. | I'm waiting for the year's first clean sheet from the sky.
dlg resident.hub : You get the aloud part of my attention. The count can stay quiet.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, your name already has a tidy place in my reckoning.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : I've run the day down to its quietest strokes.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : No need to dress it up. I can add a plain statement.
dlg resident.job [self.job=none self.trade_words] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I keep at the handle till the sound changes.
dlg resident.job : I like work that gives me one good honest thing to put down at the finish.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : The part I counted on my own ears was #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I've counted no evidence beyond the telling.
dlg resident.bye : Go with the right number of errands still in your pocket.

graft resident.hub
choice Does a fixed count make butter? -> churn_count
node churn_count
say I wish it did. I'd do the arithmetic over breakfast. Cream has its moods. The count is for the wolf on the handle.
free
choice What do you count once it turns? -> churn_count_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node churn_count_again
say One more stroke to make certain. Then I count how many clean boards are ready to take it.
choice I'll leave you to the last stroke. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
